Ω> // Lane 8 usability trace: a new user, starting only from `help`.
Ω> help
Omega Visor commands (classes: inspection, pure-execution, simulation, effect-request):
  help [command]                       inspection      list commands, or show one
  quit                                 inspection      leave the console
  inspect <x>                          inspection      show the object a name or id refers to
  type <x>                             inspection      show the type of an object
  id <x>                               inspection      show the semantic id of a name, _ or hex id
  graph <x>                            inspection      show the semantic graph reachable from x
  verify <x>                           pure-execution  run the verification pipeline on x
  machine                              inspection      show the current machine model
  realize <x> [for current.machine]    pure-execution  build machine code for x (does not run it)
  cost <x>                             simulation      estimate the cost of x
  run <x> [args...]                    pure-execution  run x if pure; effects become an effect request
  evidence [name]                      inspection      show recorded evidence receipts
  bindings                             inspection      list session names in the order they were made
  clear                                inspection      forget all session names and objects
  world [cap]                          inspection      show the runtime world state (read only)
  effects [x]                          effect-request  show effect objects as requests (never executed)
  alternatives <x>                     simulation      list other ways to realize x
  compare <a> <b>                      simulation      compare two objects or realizations
  why <x>                              inspection      explain where x came from
  let x: u64 = <expr> | fn .. | <expr> pure-execution  Omega source line, evaluated by the language
Names: a session name, _ (last result), or a semantic id (64 hex, optional sha256: prefix).
